repo,EngineKnowledge.md,58,regen,Evidence-only scan found room respawnMinutes and monster respawnHours/regen fields. No global world reset schedule or cleanup deletion policy was promoted. Hidden item behavior remains documented only until runtime/reverse-engineered evidence confirms Search/stat mechanics.
repo,EngineKnowledge.md,109,36,- Host tick timer exists and defaults to 36 Hz when enabled.
repo,EngineKnowledge.md,113,rtkick,- `RTKICK` references: 44.
repo,EngineKnowledge.md,114,begin_polling,- `BEGIN_POLLING` references: 12.
repo,EngineKnowledge.md,131,rtkick,- MajorMUD registers multiple background routines through host scheduler mechanisms (`RTKICK` / `_MY_RTKICK`).
repo,EngineKnowledge.md,149,rtkick,"- MBBSEmu host evidence supports module lifecycle, polling, RTKICK, Btrieve/storage, user/channel, event, and timer concepts."
repo,EngineKnowledge.md,156,rtkick,- Host/module polling and RTKICK-style scheduling are now validated for documentation-level modeling through MBBSEmu host evidence and MajorMUD disassembly references.
repo,EngineKnowledge.md,167,rtkick,- RTKICK is a delayed one-shot scheduling primitive measured in seconds and removed after execution.
repo,EngineKnowledge.md,168,begin_polling,- BEGIN_POLLING is a persistent polling primitive that runs until STOP_POLLING.
repo,EngineKnowledge.md,185,rtkick;begin_polling,"Promotion state remains unchanged from Validation0006: host cleanup lifecycle, RTKICK one-shot scheduling, BEGIN_POLLING persistent polling, and search/hidden-discovery subsystem are validated at engine-documentation level only. Exact cleanup flags, exact monster respawn scheduler behavior, exact search formula, and quest persistence fields remain unresolved."
repo,EngineKnowledge.md,202,rtkick,- MajorMUD has a dedicated background monster creation routine (`_BACKGROUND_MONSTER_CREATE`) that calls the monster generation driver and re-registers itself through `_MY_RTKICK`.
repo,EngineKnowledge.md,203,rtkick,- MBBSEmu confirms RTKICK semantics as one-shot delayed callbacks; repeated background behavior must be re-registered by the module.
