repo,Docs/Architecture/PROJECT_ROADMAP.md,115,36,"CodeUpdate-0036 adds knowledge-base, design-decision, reference-source, and discussion-recap documentation through direct GitHub commits."
repo,Docs/Architecture/PROJECT_ROADMAP.md,117,36,CodeUpdate-0037 combines the 0036B continuity cleanup package with the 0037 Software Design Specification package. It adds draft `Docs/SDS/` planning records and repairs stale continuity. It does not implement runtime systems.
repo,Docs/Architecture/PROJECT_ROADMAP.md,169,36,"CodeUpdate-0062 adds read-only Server scheduler bootstrap diagnostics. It registers ten disabled diagnostic channels and preserves curated ServerSim0036 planning evidence under `Docs/ServerSim/ServerSim0036/`. No scheduler ticking, sockets, sessions, gameplay, runtime rule execution, mode/profile activation, combat, movement, spawning, status-effect ticking, script dispatch, AI, character creation, world simulation, networking expansion, live editor behavior, canonical `Data/` rewrite, imported/"
repo,Docs/Architecture/PROJECT_ROADMAP.md,201,36,- CodeUpdate-0036: knowledge-base and design-decision documentation.
repo,Docs/CodeUpdates/CodeUpdate-0035-Server-Bootstrap-Validation-Summary.md,32,36,"After CodeUpdate-0035 is pushed and green, CodeUpdate-0036 should be another small approved host/server improvement."
repo,Docs/CodeUpdates/CodeUpdate-0036-Knowledge-Base-And-Design-Decisions.md,1,36,# CodeUpdate-0036 - Knowledge Base and Design Decisions
repo,Docs/CodeUpdates/CodeUpdate-0036-Knowledge-Base-And-Design-Decisions.md,5,36,"CodeUpdate-0036 records the major design, research, and reference-source decisions discussed after CodeUpdate-0035. This is a documentation-only update. It does not add runtime gameplay systems, combat, character creation, world simulation, networking expansion, or editor implementation."
repo,Docs/CodeUpdates/CodeUpdate-0036-Knowledge-Base-And-Design-Decisions.md,49,36,"After CodeUpdate-0036 is pushed and GitHub Actions is green by user report, CodeUpdate-0037 should be approved by the user before implementation. A safe candidate is a planning or foundation slice for gameplay flags, quest data modeling, or host/admin permissions, still without broad gameplay implementation unless explicitly approved."
repo,Docs/CodeUpdates/CodeUpdate-0037-Software-Design-Specification.md,5,36,CodeUpdate-0037 combines the user-provided CodeUpdate-0036B continuity cleanup package with the user-provided CodeUpdate-0037 Software Design Specification package.
