repo,Documentation/RuntimeTraceHarness/RuntimeTraceHarness0080.md,17,regen,5. World iteration — captures player/session/NPC/combat/regen/quest/spawn update order.
repo,Documentation/RuntimeTraceHarness/RuntimeTraceExecution0081.md,9,timer.hertz,"1. **Scheduler cadence is host-controlled.** MBBSEmu uses a `Timer.Hertz` event when idle, but bypasses waiting when session input, output, or processing is pending. This supports host/module-driven timing, not modem-ping-driven gameplay ticks."
repo,Documentation/RuntimeTraceHarness/RuntimeTraceExecution0081.md,13,rtkick;rtihdlr;syscyc;initask,3. **MBBSEmu timed callback order is reconstructed:** `RTKICK` → `RTIHDLR` → `SYSCYC` → `INITASK`/tasks.
repo,Documentation/RuntimeTraceHarness/RuntimeTraceExecution0081.md,15,rtihdlr,"4. **RTIHDLR has a ~55ms gate in MBBSEmu.** This is host evidence, not proof MajorMUD uses RTIHDLR."
repo,Documentation/RuntimeTraceHarness/RuntimeTraceExecution0081.md,17,ticker,"5. **GSBL `TICKER` increments once per second.** This is a visible host/GSBL timing variable, but not automatically the gameplay tick."
