repo,Reports/Validation0009/Validation0009-MonsterRespawnSchedulerTargetedRerun.md,20,rtkick,"`_BACKGROUND_MONSTER_CREATE` is a dedicated MajorMUD background routine. It calls `sub_26DF7`, then re-registers itself using `_MY_RTKICK` with `word_998E8` as the delay value. This supports a recurring background monster creation loop implemented as repeated one-shot RTKICK scheduling."
repo,Reports/Validation0009/Validation0009-MonsterRespawnSchedulerTargetedRerun.md,24,rtkick,### RTKICK semantics
repo,Reports/Validation0009/Validation0009-MonsterRespawnSchedulerTargetedRerun.md,26,rtkick,MBBSEmu documents and implements RTKICK routines as delayed callbacks that execute once and are then discarded. The MajorMUD disassembly's `_MY_RTKICK` wrapper inserts callbacks into an ordered scheduled-list structure using the current tick counter plus the requested delay. This validates that repeated background behavior must be re-registered after each execution.
